{"step_index":1134,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T19:15:55Z","thinking":"**Analyzing WPF Exit**\n\nI'm stumped. Every run of Spectra.exe follows the same sequence: it loads MainWindow, initializes WebView2, navigates, and *then* cleanly exits. The mystery remains: why does WPF terminate immediately after MainWindow_Loaded completes? The expected behavior is not happening.\n\n\n**Investigating WPF Behavior**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the WPF window lifecycle and some unusual window properties in the XAML. The `ShowInTaskbar=\"False\"` and `WindowStyle=\"None\"` settings are especially interesting. My hypothesis is that, absent activation or focus, these properties may contribute to the unexpected shutdown behavior. I'm focusing on how `App.ShutdownMode` might be interacting with these settings, and I believe I'm getting closer to the root cause.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra\\web\\js\\main.js","EndLine":100,"StartLine":1,"toolAction":"Viewing main.js","toolSummary":"View main.js"}}]}
