{"step_index":1199,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T19:19:40Z","thinking":"**Investigating Process Termination**\n\nI'm puzzled, `ProcessExit` didn't fire. I need to understand under what specific conditions, particularly in a Windows environment, a process can terminate abruptly, bypassing crucial events like `ProcessExit`, `AppDomain.UnhandledException`, `Application.Exit`, and `Window.Closed`. It seems there are only two real possibilities, and I am close to having identified them.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Culprit**\n\nI've narrowed it down to `TerminateProcess` calls, fast fails, or user/Windows termination. I've been examining the native code execution at the moment of termination and zeroed in on the `SetWindowDisplayAffinity` call within `ApplyCaptureProtection`. The crucial log entry for `[CaptureProtection] Applied` never appears, strongly suggesting that `SetWindowDisplayAffinity` is the breaking point.\n\n\n**Analyzing the DWM Conflict**\n\nI've determined `SetWindowDisplayAffinity`'s interaction with active WebView2 GPU acceleration is the issue. Calling it on a window with D3D-presented child surfaces (from WebView2) triggers hardware device removal errors or access violations in DWM/D3D11.dll. The WPF window handle (`helper.Handle`) is the top-level window, but WebView2's child windows (`Chrome_WidgetWin_0`, `Intermediate D3D Window`) are where the conflict arises, preventing the expected log entry for capture protection from appearing.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Comment out ApplyCaptureProtection in NavigationCompleted for test.","EndLine":142,"Instruction":"Comment out ApplyCaptureProtection in NavigationCompleted","ReplacementContent":"                WebView.NavigationCompleted += (s, args) =>\n                {\n                    File.AppendAllText(LogPath, $\"[WebView2 NavigationCompleted] Success={args.IsSuccess}, ErrorStatus={args.WebErrorStatus}\\n\");\n                    // Testing window stability without SetWindowDisplayAffinity call\n                };","StartLine":129,"TargetContent":"                WebView.NavigationCompleted += (s, args) =>\n                {\n                    File.AppendAllText(LogPath, $\"[WebView2 NavigationCompleted] Success={args.IsSuccess}, ErrorStatus={args.WebErrorStatus}\\n\");\n                    if (args.IsSuccess)\n                    {\n                        Dispatcher.InvokeAsync(async () =>\n                        {\n                            await Task.Delay(500);\n                            bool cap = _windowManager.ApplyCaptureProtection();\n                            File.AppendAllText(LogPath, $\"[CaptureProtection] Applied={cap}\\n\");\n                        });\n                    }\n                };","TargetFile":"c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra\\src-csharp\\UI\\MainWindow.xaml.cs","toolAction":"Disabling ApplyCaptureProtection for isolation test","toolSummary":"Update MainWindow.xaml.cs"}}]}
